error[E1002]: `xs[i + 1]` cannot go `mut` here: it overlaps `xs[i]`, already passed `mut` in this call
 --> mem:///main.lu:8:43
  |
8 |     add3(mut xs[i], { i = i - 1; 0 }, mut xs[i + 1])
  |              ----- `xs[i]` is passed `mut` here
  |                                           ^^^^^^^^^ second exclusive claim on the same place
  |
  = note: `xs[i]` and `xs[i + 1]` may be one element: an index that is not a literal is one place
    with every other index of its container; only two different literals, two offsets `i +
    a` and `i + b` of one local the call leaves unwritten, and a loop index over literal
    bounds against a literal outside them are distinct [mem.model.place.elem].
